**Discriminating-power requirement (binds E3–E7).** Every one of these is computed *from* the schema and
*from* the goals; none can be satisfied without both being real. That is the property that distinguishes
this evidence from CANARY-0002's `echo`: the result differs depending on whether §4.3 and the corpus are
what they claim to be. E5 in particular cannot be satisfied by prose — it counts cells against a
denominator derived independently at WU-3.

**Not covered — stated, not hidden.** Single-rater extraction (assumption A5): no inter-rater agreement
statistic (DESIGN §6 G3). Acceptable for a spike; if the result is used to justify *building* SAKG, a
second rater on ≥1 goal is warranted. And `n = 3` is fixed by the objective: it supports a NO-GO (one
structural absence is a real finding) far better than a GO (three clean goals is weak evidence the schema
generalizes) — an asymmetry any reader of an eventual GO must hold onto (DESIGN §6 G4).

