## 4. Rollback plan

No code ships and no service is deployed, so rollback is *evidential*: the risk is a corrupted or
un-retractable finding entering the gate, not a broken build. The artifact is a single file; the
dangerous states are ones where it looks valid but is not.

### 4.1 Per-unit rollback

| unit | rollback | cost |
|---|---|---|
| WU-0 | none needed — grant is additive; revoke by ending the session | free |
| WU-1 | discard audit block; re-run | free |
| WU-2 | revert the criterion **only before WU-3 begins** (§4.2) | free pre-WU-3, forbidden after |
| WU-3 | rebuild `F` from §4.3; if `|F|` changes, **WU-5 and WU-6 are void** and re-run in full | high — full re-extraction |
| WU-4 | see §4.3 — not a free rollback | disclosure-bearing |
| WU-5 | re-score affected cells; recompute WU-6/7. Cell-level correction with a stated reason is legitimate | low, if disclosed |
| WU-6 | pure function — recompute; no state to unwind | free |
| WU-7 | pure function — recompute | free |
| WU-8 | `rm reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md` and re-emit. Safe **only** if the file has not yet been consumed by a gate or cited downstream; if it has, supersede with a new dated artifact and a retraction note rather than deleting | free → moderate |
| WU-9 | n/a — read-only check | free |

### 4.2 Irreversibility: the criteria freeze
Once WU-3 starts, WU-2 is closed. Amending accept criteria after data has been touched is
indistinguishable from tuning the gate to the result. If a criterion defect is discovered mid-probe,
the rollback is **not** to amend it — it is to complete the probe under the criteria as frozen and
record the defect in `## analysis` for the next cycle.

### 4.3 Irreversibility: the sample lock
`G` is locked at WU-4. Re-running selection after seeing any downstream output — cells, score, or
verdict — does not restore a clean state; it converts the probe into a search for an agreeable sample.
If it happens for any reason, the **only** valid recovery is to emit with `sample_reselected: true` in
the frontmatter and state why in `## analysis`. Silent re-selection is the failure mode this lock
exists to make visible. Directionality is the integrity property (DESIGN §2): C5 must never reach back
and revise C2 or C3.

### 4.4 Global abort
If at any point the probe cannot proceed on **real** inputs, abort — do not substitute invented goals.
Terminal states are `EMIT(GO)`, `EMIT(NO-GO)`, `ABORT(<reason>)`. `ABORT` ≠ `NO-GO`: NO-GO means the
probe ran and §9/A8 failed; ABORT means the probe could not run and carries no evidential weight about
§9/A8 either way. Recording an abort as NO-GO is a **false falsification**; recording it as GO is
**fabricated evidence** (`CANARY-0001` framing). An aborted probe writes its abort reason to the same
path so the failure is legible, with **no** `verdict:` line — which correctly fails accept predicate 2
rather than smuggling a null result past the gate.

### 4.5 Rollback of *this* plan
`plan/` is not TCB (`constitution/` is the immutable Z0 layer, amend-only via `kernel/amendment.py`).
This file is freely revisable **until WU-3 begins**; after that, the pre-registered content — §3.4
selection rule, the 0.30 threshold, the veto rule — is frozen for the current probe run and changes
apply only to the next one. Revisions after freeze must be recorded as a new plan version, not an
in-place edit, so that what was pre-registered stays legible.

