## 5. Assumptions carried into execution

Inherited from DESIGN §1, all still unverified — `spec/` remains unreadable from PLAN. Each is
discharged or falsified at the WU noted, cheaply and early rather than inherited silently.

| # | assumption | discharged at | if false |
|---|---|---|---|
| A1 | §4.3 is a closed, finite set of node types with named fields | WU-1(b), WU-3 | no scoring denominator → `ABORT(schema-undefined)`; instrument needs redesign, not reparameterization |
| A2 | §9/A8 asserts sealed goals are (near-)losslessly extractable into §4.3 | WU-1(c) | probe faithfully measures the wrong proposition — **quote §9/A8 verbatim before scoring** |
| A3 | "sealed" is determinate and queryable | WU-1(d) | selection becomes a researcher degree of freedom; pre-registration void |
| A4 | ≥3 sealed goals exist | WU-1(e) | `NO-GO(insufficient-corpus)` — do not pad |
| A5 | per-field verdict is judgeable by one reader | WU-5 | single-rater loss ratio not defensible; needs second rater + agreement stat |
| A6 | loss ratio is unweighted mean field fidelity | WU-6 | aggregate meaningless if fields differ in criticality — mitigated by the veto |
| A7 | the 3 goals should be heterogeneous | WU-4 | homogeneous sample inflates fidelity and manufactures a GO |

A2 and A7 remain the two most likely to silently invalidate the probe: A2 because the instrument can
measure the wrong proposition perfectly, A7 because it is the unforced path to a false GO.

